From 832bfe9efa2d570420d6f560c1be3e7df88bbd87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtualAxe <virtualaxe@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 13:07:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nerdnos: precompute virtual nonce search material

Why: NerdNos live smoke phases reached API health, assigned pool difficulty, and virtual ASIC work but sometimes failed to produce a submit within the smoke window. Precomputing invariant SHA-256 header material keeps the guest-side virtual ASIC fast enough for low-difficulty live proof without moving work to the host.

Virtual-only: only the VIRTUALAXE_GAMMA virtual ASIC search implementation changes. Physical NerdNos ASIC paths keep using their existing hardware result flow.

Upstream surface: NerdNos virtual ASIC SHA cache, candidate filter, and nonce-difficulty calculation.

Verify: SOURCE=nerdnos make patch-check, SOURCE=nerdnos make verify-submit-replay, python3 scripts/virtualaxe.py verify-test-ci --source nerdnos --json, and make verify-release SOURCE=nerdnos.

Removal impact: live low-difficulty pool phases remain probabilistic because the
virtual ASIC recomputes full header hashes for every nonce.
